              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ملل — malal — \"boredom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شعر الطالب بالملل في المحاضرة الطويلة. shaʿara aṭ-ṭālib bi-l-malal fī al-muḥāḍara aṭ-ṭawīla. The student felt bored in the long lecture."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic says شعر بالملل, to feel boredom, where English says to be bored."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ملل (malal) is built on the native Arabic root m-l-l, \"to be weary of a thing\" (Lane). Malal is the noun of that weariness."
            }
          ]
        },
