              "text": "غضب — ghaḍiba — \"to get angry\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "غضب أبي لأن أخي كسر النافذة. ghaḍiba abī li-anna akhī kasara an-nāfidha. My father got angry because my brother broke the window."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يغضب, yaghḍab."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes من for the person: غضب (ghaḍiba) من أخيه."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "غضب (ghaḍiba) is built on the native Arabic root gh-ḍ-b, \"anger, wrath\" (Lane). The adjective ghāḍib, angry, and the noun ghaḍab, anger, come from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
